|n^|a|lg|f|at|^c@2
To get the best out of aaBridge you need the DDS to be available.  Try installing|fp|t-40|at|^*b Java 8^*n|fp||at| from Oracle.
At the time of writing (early 2025) the link below is a good place to look.|
lg|k|at|
^c    ^*Hhttps://www.java.com/en/download/manual.jsp^*n       links directly to Oracle Java 8.
|lg|f|n#|4|at|To see which Java is powering aaBridge ^*b click ^*n on the ^*b Show ^*n tab, top of the  right-hand  column.
Next look for |cp|green|at|^*b Java Version ^*n|cp||at| lower in that column. It also shows your H/W type e.g. |cp|blue|at|^*bintel64^*n|cp||at|  or  |cp|red|at|^*baarch^*n|cp||at| (ARM).
|n#|8|at|The above link provides ^*bJava 8^*n for all Windows and all Macs and MOST Linux OSes. 
The ^*bONE and ONLY^*n exception is that if you are running ^*bLINUX^*n on |cp|red|at|^*bARM^*n|cp||at| hardware. e.g. Mac M Chips or the Snapdragon processor then you will need a native Java 8 for that Linux OS. |
lg|m|at|
For example - if you are running ^*b Ubuntu 24 ^*n the terminal command
       ^*bsudo apt-get install openjdk-8-jdk ^*n
is what you need.

^bNote - Newer Java's (the latest is v23) will also run the DDS just fine, (but some ^*bLinux^*n's, may have issues).|



